WEBVTT

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:24.370
Oh, hey Rygart.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:26.170
What are you up to?

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:28.650
Hey, you—

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:31.010
Get back here, asshole!

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:33.880
I'll bring you back a nice souvenir from the capital!

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:38.220
That idiot took off so he wouldn't
have to help with the harvest.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.720
Not likes there's anything good waiting for him.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:59.330
The Continent of Cruzon.
A place where oil isn't found in the land.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:06.790
People of the land are born with a certain ability:

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:10.020
The ability to freely control quartz.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:15.390
They refine quartz with high flexibility

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:19.260
and create ligaments that can expand and contract at will.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:24.230
The ligament control the movement of vehicles,

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:26.230
makes wheels spin,

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:31.230
and push pistons for compressing air and firing bullets.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:38.900
People of varying strengths hold
the power to control quartz.

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:43.400
People refer to their ability as magic.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:27.120
Daddy?

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:30.670
Aren't there any lighters?

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:32.630
I'm sorry, Mr Arrow.

00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:35.290
Even two year olds can levitate these.

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:39.330
If he can't even do it as a five year old,

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:41.720
then he's...

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:44.650
an un-sorcerer.

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:44.150
Rygart Arrow?

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:46.490
King Hodr has summoned you.

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:50.410
Water... W-Water...

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:57.450
I didn't think I'd really find you collapsed here,

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:00.290
but King Hodr was right.

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:08.790
Well, I can't use anything that moves with magic.

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:11.040
I'm sure that's how he figured I'd be around here.

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:12.880
He's a clever guy.

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:18.180
So it wasn't just a myth.

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:20.090
You really can't use magic.

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:24.180
Well, sorry about that.

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:27.770
No, it's just you're the first one I've met in my life.

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:30.600
I apologize if I offended you.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:32.520
Nah, I'm used to it.

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:34.600
So, who are you?

00:05:35.070 --> 00:05:37.780
I'm Baldr, a general of the Krisna Kingdom.

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:41.320
G-General? Oh...

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:06.800
Give me a clear line of sight!

00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:15.650
Go around it!

00:06:18.170 --> 00:06:19.700
Soldiers, get back!

00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:30.700
You Athens soldier. This is for—

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:40.750
Just two shots?

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:43.710
That's one enormous bullet.

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:49.010
I can't reach.

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:50.150
They're shooting from outside my range.

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:04.190
Fall back! Retreat!

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:07.110
Are you okay?

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:09.110
Y-Yes.

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:12.250
I'm sorry, Zess.

00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:13.600
Captain Zess!

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:17.260
Cleo! Get up already.

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:18.870
I was just about to!

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:24.830
Lee, I landed one of my shots!

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:26.850
Landed on what?

00:07:26.850 --> 00:07:28.090
The enemies.

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:30.340
You just got lucky.

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:36.550
They only brought out three archaic Golems
when we're a fair way into their kingdom.

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:41.600
It wouldn't matter if they fought our nation
head to head. We're five times as powerful.

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:43.350
They wouldn't stand a chance.

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:47.090
I'm sure they've focused their units
on their capital and the border wall.

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:52.340
Let's go.

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:03.700
The capital, Binonten!

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:05.830
We're here!

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:13.700
General Baldr! Welcome back!

00:08:13.700 --> 00:08:15.400
Thanks for keeping watch.

00:08:18.850 --> 00:08:21.680
Oh, you're really a general?

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:23.910
Guess what, Mom?

00:08:23.910 --> 00:08:25.730
I was the best one in my class.

00:08:25.910 --> 00:08:27.430
Really?

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:34.600
Listen up, this only costs 3000 yen!

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:38.840
Rygart, is this your first time here?

00:08:38.840 --> 00:08:41.890
No, I came here once when I was a kid.

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:43.790
My dad brought me.

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:51.070
Queen Sigyn.

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:54.000
What should I do here?

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:57.530
If you don't leave some space open,
it'll become difficult to—

00:08:58.350 --> 00:08:59.730
Queen Sigyn?

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:03.420
Rygart Arrow!

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:05.450
Si—

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:10.860
Si-Sigyn.

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:15.290
Why didn't you come to Hodr's and my wedding?

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:20.020
I was... busy with some stuff.

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:25.270
What's more important than your best friends' wedding?

00:09:25.270 --> 00:09:28.450
I could name lots of things! Like the harvest.

00:09:28.450 --> 00:09:30.990
So it's not that you don't like us?

00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:32.710
Of course it's not.

00:09:34.820 --> 00:09:36.050
Geez...

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:38.400
I haven't seen you for four years and this is how you greet me?

00:09:42.430 --> 00:09:45.330
I'm so happy to see you, Rygart.

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:50.180
Look at Queen Sigyn's smile!

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:51.990
Who is that guy anyway?

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:55.890
He's a friend of the King and Queen from back when they were students.

00:09:56.110 --> 00:10:01.570
He's one of those un-sorcerers
who's born once in a million years.

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:04.810
I wonder how he's survived without using magic.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:09.870
What I want to know is why the King summoned him.

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:13.800
Maybe he wants to reminisce on his past.

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:21.630
King Hodr, I've brought Sir Rygart.

00:10:24.050 --> 00:10:25.050
Huh?

00:10:25.050 --> 00:10:27.660
Thanks for coming.

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:30.290
Check out my chair.

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:31.870
Hodr.

00:10:33.170 --> 00:10:37.230
As his wife and a citizen, what do you think
about a king who doesn't like his throne?

00:10:37.230 --> 00:10:39.010
I heard you, citizen.

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:42.150
For insulting the king, you'll pay with your life.

00:10:43.550 --> 00:10:48.180
I spent five whole days to get
here after reading your message,

00:10:48.220 --> 00:10:49.770
and that's how you treat me?

00:10:58.980 --> 00:11:01.090
Gram, you've gotten bigger.

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:03.640
Thanks for coming, Rygart.

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:07.280
Man, if you're gonna call me here, you should at least tell me why.

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:13.450
Is the Troublemaker Quartet of Assam
Military School going to have a reunion?

00:11:13.830 --> 00:11:14.770
Troublemaker?

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:20.630
Yep! A prince who was always looking at the sky
to lose some points and avoid the throne,

00:11:21.130 --> 00:11:22.920
a mad scientist who locked herself up in the school's lab

00:11:22.920 --> 00:11:25.850
for three days and nights,
no sleep, no food, no water and—

00:11:25.850 --> 00:11:26.700
The King of Make-ups.

00:11:29.850 --> 00:11:32.430
Then Zess, who we call Mr. Uptight,
completes the quartet.

00:11:32.890 --> 00:11:33.880
You called him here, too, right?

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:39.210
Don't you know?

00:11:40.280 --> 00:11:43.810
One month ago, there was a coup d'etat in Assam.

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:51.450
Athens and Orlando both made armed
interventions and it resulted in Athens' victory.

00:11:52.330 --> 00:11:55.290
Basically, Assam isn't neutral anymore.

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:57.530
It belongs to the Athens.

00:11:58.750 --> 00:12:02.300
So the neighboring countries were at war and none of the news ever reached me.

00:12:02.710 --> 00:12:04.930
It's not simply a neighboring issue anymore.

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:08.600
I haven't disclosed the news to the citizens yet, but...

00:12:11.640 --> 00:12:16.900
Our Krisnan Army and the Athens Commonwealth are already fighting at the city border.

00:12:17.480 --> 00:12:19.720
The defense of the Mizoram Stronghold is tough,

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:24.030
but I've also received a report that a small platoon
has broken through the grand canyon in the north.

00:12:28.270 --> 00:12:30.370
And the captain of that platoon is Zess.

00:12:31.700 --> 00:12:32.990
Zess?!

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:34.660
No, that's impossible!

00:12:35.160 --> 00:12:39.270
I mean, I know he's from Athens, and he was also a prodigy pilot,

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:42.180
but he hated war more than anyone!

00:12:44.670 --> 00:12:47.150
He enlisted to the army

00:12:47.150 --> 00:12:51.470
because he wanted to stop his brother
who's the Commander of Athens, right?

00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:06.490
The Mizoram Stronghold is holding out well, but...

00:13:07.240 --> 00:13:11.030
it's only a matter of time until they break through that too.

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:14.230
What's up?

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:16.950
Thanks for the valuable information.

00:13:16.950 --> 00:13:19.200
Before all of Krisna becomes a battlefield

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:21.840
I'll be running away into the
mountains with my little brother.

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:23.230
Run away?

00:13:23.230 --> 00:13:24.650
You brainless coward!

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:25.600
Silence!

00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:26.670
Sir...

00:13:27.670 --> 00:13:28.630
Hodr?

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:31.170
Rygart.

00:13:31.550 --> 00:13:33.280
I need your help.

00:13:34.470 --> 00:13:35.620
You know my strength.

00:13:35.930 --> 00:13:37.930
I can't even fire a normal rifle.

00:13:38.390 --> 00:13:39.290
Come with me.

00:13:44.610 --> 00:13:45.480
Queen Sigyn.

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:49.550
His Highness seems to trust him very much.

00:13:49.550 --> 00:13:50.570
May I know who he is?

00:13:50.950 --> 00:13:53.580
He is a friend from back when we were students.

00:13:54.450 --> 00:13:57.700
Well, he doesn't seem to be just any colleague.

00:13:57.700 --> 00:13:58.700
Yes.

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:03.190
He's the only man who could stop a fight

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:07.320
between the Commander of Athens'
brother and the prince of a kingdom.

00:14:09.340 --> 00:14:10.720
He's a rather odd person.

00:14:12.680 --> 00:14:13.920
An odd person?

00:14:15.390 --> 00:14:15.970
Yes.

00:14:18.300 --> 00:14:19.270
King Hodr!

00:14:19.270 --> 00:14:20.250
Your Highness!

00:14:21.230 --> 00:14:24.080
Rygart, is your father well?

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:26.520
Oh, he passed away last year.

00:14:26.520 --> 00:14:27.500
What?!

00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:30.030
What about his funeral?
Why didn't you invite me?

00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:31.820
We didn't have a funeral.

00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:33.500
No one would've come anyway.

00:14:33.950 --> 00:14:39.040
He raised two un-sorcerers and went into debt putting me through military school.

00:14:39.450 --> 00:14:41.530
He truly thought my power would awaken.

00:14:42.670 --> 00:14:44.040
A fool, if you ask me.

00:14:44.830 --> 00:14:46.960
I'd say he's an admirable father.

00:14:48.840 --> 00:14:50.800
He picked a fight with fate.

00:14:52.090 --> 00:14:52.760
I..

00:14:55.930 --> 00:14:56.990
couldn't.

00:15:32.050 --> 00:15:33.760
It's... a Golem, right?

00:15:35.470 --> 00:15:39.900
We dug this up last month when we were mining for quartz.

00:15:39.900 --> 00:15:41.970
We suspect it to be a millennium old.

00:15:42.730 --> 00:15:45.100
Under-Golem, you may call it.

00:15:46.770 --> 00:15:47.960
A millennium old?

00:15:53.900 --> 00:15:55.490
Distance to Binonten?

00:15:55.490 --> 00:15:56.800
About 1200.

00:15:57.700 --> 00:15:59.870
Sigyn's been really intrigued by this.

00:16:00.490 --> 00:16:02.320
That's why I called you here.

00:16:07.080 --> 00:16:08.910
It's the ancient who was in the Golem.

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:13.840
Much to our surprise, that ancient doesn't
have a trace of ever controlling quartz.

00:16:14.170 --> 00:16:18.330
Basically, this Golem doesn't mobilize with magic.

00:16:20.060 --> 00:16:25.640
I had several high-rank pilots try,
but not a single one could activate it.

00:16:26.940 --> 00:16:29.990
This is nothing more than a Golem mechanic's theory,

00:16:30.350 --> 00:16:32.980
but the ancients may have been unable to use magic

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:37.320
and used a different method to pilot Golems.

00:16:38.700 --> 00:16:40.160
A different method?

00:16:40.850 --> 00:16:44.790
Rygart, can you help research this Golem?

00:16:44.950 --> 00:16:45.960
Me?

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:51.340
If we can further analyze this Golem,
we may be able to strengthen our own Golems.

00:16:52.590 --> 00:16:53.840
Hey, Hodr.

00:16:54.170 --> 00:16:56.590
Are you really going to fight a war with Athens?

00:16:57.050 --> 00:16:59.090
You're no match for them.

00:16:59.090 --> 00:17:00.460
Let's surrender!

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:02.350
I wouldn't say this in front of anyone else, but...

00:17:02.850 --> 00:17:04.840
I agree with the idea of surrendering.

00:17:07.020 --> 00:17:07.700
What was that?

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:14.340
Athens has proposed a peace treaty.

00:17:15.240 --> 00:17:16.740
Then you can come in terms!

00:17:16.740 --> 00:17:18.030
Under the conditions

00:17:18.850 --> 00:17:22.160
of surrendering the entire territory to Athens

00:17:22.660 --> 00:17:25.350
and the divestment of all noble ranks...

00:17:27.470 --> 00:17:30.920
We're under attack!
We're closing the border gate! Go back!

00:17:31.750 --> 00:17:33.270
Then let's surrender.

00:17:33.270 --> 00:17:34.710
Those conditions are nothing.

00:17:34.710 --> 00:17:40.220
You also used to say that it's
ridiculous to choose a ruler through inheritance.

00:17:41.300 --> 00:17:42.580
And...

00:17:44.510 --> 00:17:46.400
Where are they firing from?

00:17:46.400 --> 00:17:48.450
What's going on?

00:17:51.600 --> 00:17:54.490
The execution of the Krisnan Royal Family.

00:17:56.690 --> 00:17:59.450
Sigyn wasn't born a royal, but it includes her too.

00:18:02.490 --> 00:18:06.370
In front of Sigyn and the Prime Minister,
I must act as a king.

00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:09.740
Rygart, please tell me.

00:18:11.210 --> 00:18:12.230
What...

00:18:13.710 --> 00:18:15.300
should I do?

00:18:22.840 --> 00:18:25.220
They're firing from between two
and five o'clock, at least 200 away.

00:18:25.310 --> 00:18:26.470
200?!

00:18:30.050 --> 00:18:32.100
They seem to have figured out our location.

00:18:32.270 --> 00:18:34.610
Okay. Cleo, go back to your Golem.

00:18:35.150 --> 00:18:36.400
Roger.

00:18:39.940 --> 00:18:44.950
They didn't write out the last condition.
They had their messenger tell me in person.

00:18:46.370 --> 00:18:47.550
Hats off to the Commander.

00:18:47.550 --> 00:18:51.370
Commander Loquis wants to take us over,
not get on friendly terms.

00:18:55.710 --> 00:18:56.600
That's your problem!

00:18:56.600 --> 00:18:59.110
That's what Zess was always so pissed about!

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:03.400
You act like it doesn't concern you even when your life is in danger!

00:19:03.400 --> 00:19:05.800
As if you've already given up!

00:19:06.550 --> 00:19:07.380
Sorry.

00:19:07.720 --> 00:19:09.020
Don't apologize.

00:19:09.220 --> 00:19:10.680
I'm not mad.

00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:17.400
In any case, we can't fulfill that stupid condition!

00:19:19.280 --> 00:19:20.900
Your Majesty!

00:19:20.900 --> 00:19:21.900
We're under attack!

00:19:32.410 --> 00:19:33.500
Rygart!

00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:35.410
Your Majesty, are you okay?

00:19:35.540 --> 00:19:36.540
Rygart!

00:19:42.130 --> 00:19:44.030
Your Majesty, you must evacuate to the castle.

00:19:44.430 --> 00:19:45.330
But Rygart's—

00:19:46.140 --> 00:19:49.380
Go! You're the king for God's sake!

00:19:50.140 --> 00:19:51.430
Please, hurry!

00:19:52.930 --> 00:19:54.900
Hang in there! We'll come right back to save you.

00:19:55.850 --> 00:19:57.770
Sure, thanks!

00:20:07.370 --> 00:20:08.730
You're such a pain.

00:20:16.830 --> 00:20:19.580
H-How do I open this thing?

00:20:25.510 --> 00:20:27.510
Is this... quartz?

00:20:27.970 --> 00:20:31.310
No, then it wouldn't respond to me.

00:20:31.970 --> 00:20:33.320
What the...

00:20:33.320 --> 00:20:34.370
Letters?

00:20:39.150 --> 00:20:40.320
Please, hold!

00:20:46.450 --> 00:20:47.820
There's more of you?

00:20:47.820 --> 00:20:50.630
Fine, I'll change to anti-human bullets.

00:20:58.500 --> 00:20:59.710
Are these hieroglyphs?

00:21:00.590 --> 00:21:03.500
The smaller letters resemble the language we use.

00:21:03.880 --> 00:21:07.090
New pilot re...

00:21:08.340 --> 00:21:10.390
Who am I kidding, I can't read this.

00:21:14.600 --> 00:21:16.400
King of Krisna, Hodr!

00:21:16.600 --> 00:21:19.190
Zess, I have achieved our goal!

00:21:24.030 --> 00:21:24.940
What?

00:21:29.070 --> 00:21:30.160
What's going on?

00:21:30.160 --> 00:21:31.350
It's not making sense!

00:21:34.410 --> 00:21:36.700
Cleo! What's the enemy's response?

00:21:36.700 --> 00:21:38.530
There's no response.

00:21:57.930 --> 00:21:58.820
The ground is shaking!

00:23:50.920 --> 00:23:54.370
Don't ask me why it suddenly started moving.

00:23:55.920 --> 00:23:58.920
Under-Golem, the Ancient Giant Soldier.
